WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.570
Scrub, scrub!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.650
Blossom, let's hurry!

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.530
Right!

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.780
Let's do a simultaneous kick!

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:13.910
Got it!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:15.870
Blossom!

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.500
Marine!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.010
Well, in that case...

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.680
Gather, Floral Power!

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.390
Blossom Tact!

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.100
What's the matter?!

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.350
We have to save him!

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.980
I'm going to remove the rubble, all right?

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.490
Marine Impact!

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.370
Here I go!

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.290
Gather, Floral Power!

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.520
Marine Tact!

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.680
Flowers, glitter bright!

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:32.080
Precure Blue Forte Wave!{Blue = 1750}

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.090
So cool!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.330
Although I dunno about you...

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.400
This isn't the time to be feeling down!

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.810
We must find the Blossom Tact!

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.350
Your Tact is right here.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.380
I've heard rumors...

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.610
but the weakest Precure in history is still just as weak now that there are two of you.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.990
Weakest...

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.820
And just who are you?!

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.490
One of the Desert Apostles...

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.450
Commander Kumojacky!

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:20.990
Commander?!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.660
Please give back the Tact!

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.660
I suppose it would be boring to defeat such a weak Precure.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.140
Here you go. Consider it a present.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.090
First Sasorina, and now a new commander...

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:36.070
{OP}

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.270
HeartCatch

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.730
Precure!

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.310
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.270
Now, all together

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.780
HeartCatch Precure!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.740
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.410
Within each of our chests,

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.070
they begin to sprout

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.710
The seeds of the heart

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.010
are growing

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.620
bit by bit

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:09.290
Red,

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:09.910
white

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.210
and yellow

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.960
It's because these blooming buds are

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.380
all varied colors

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:16.840
that they

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.050
shine so brightly!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.390
That smile that you've nurtured

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.890
with such care

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.600
will never wither

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.190
HeartCatch Precure!

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.030
Now, all together

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.530
HeartCatch Precure!

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.200
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:46.070
They're always right by our sides

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:46.910
So together

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:50.790
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.750
bloom even more!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.250
HeartCatch

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.710
Precure!

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.340
I ended up causing trouble for Erika, didn't I...

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.840
Even if you're no good right now, you just have to grow one step at a time.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.360
So I <i>am</i> no good after all.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.310
Tsubomi!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.010
Good mornin'!

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.150
Morning!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.870
Good morning!

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.610
Morning.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.210
Keep your spirits up today, all right?

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.610
R-Right.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.360
It's like Erika says!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.340
I have to stay positive! {Changed 'as' to 'like.'}

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.710
The Precure Partnership

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.710
The Precure Partnership

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.840
Is that so?

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.710
Then the second Precure has finally appeared. {Boys and girls of every age, wouldn't you like to hear something strange? o/~}

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.640
Her name is Cure Marine.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.260
She seems more capable than Cure Blossom, at least. {WHOEVER WAS RESPONSIBLE FOR 'less incapable' SHOULD BE SHOT.}

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.980
Even if there are two Precure now,

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.850
I, Kumojacky, bear the strength of a hundred!

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:02.080
More importantly, Kumojacky, why did you give Blossom her Tact back?

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.170
I care not for this trivia.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.140
The only foe I care for is the world itself!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:07.700
Huh?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.480
It is true that our objective is indeed the world itself.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:15.020
We shall make the hearts of its people as barren as the desert

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.410
and then subjugate the entire world! {Changed 'the' to 'its.'}

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.670
Leave this one to me.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.030
Tsubomi, turn off the alcohol lamp, will you?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.780
Huh?! But I'm scared...

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.290
All you're doing is putting a cap on it.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.730
Capping your ears instead isn't going to help.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.390
Sheesh...

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.350
I'm sorry...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.800
We've got soccer next, right?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.070
All right then! We'll leave the cleanup to you!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:43.900
Hold it!

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.840
Why do we have to clean up after you?!

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.780
That's right!

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.200
Stop making such a huge fuss.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.860
I'm not!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:53.790
Let's settle this fairly with Rock Paper Scissors!

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.460
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

00:05:57.630 --> 00:05:58.960
Gotcha!

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.880
Yaaay!

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.550
<i>Erika really is amazing...</i>

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.010
Erika, you're so cool!

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.850
Do your best too, Tsubomi!

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.640
Right!

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:15.830
Are you all right?!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.810
I'm fine...

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.610
I'm so lame...

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.840
"He fled all alone through the window of the classroom..."

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:27.110
<i>I guess I just can't compare to Erika...</i>

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:31.020
<i>As a Precure, all I do is hold her back...</i>

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:36.500
"I lay in the grass of Kozukata Castle, my heart of fifteen drawn into the sky..."

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.540
<i>My heart of fifteen, drawn into the sky...</i>

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.080
<i>Sounds almost like me...</i>

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.410
<i>Though I'm still not fifteen yet.</i>

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:44.750
Hanasaki!

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.760
I'd like you to answer that question.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.500
Um, well...

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.450
It's Tankobu! The answer's Tankobu!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.550
It's "Tankobu"!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:57.160
It's "Takuboku"! The author's name is Ishikawa Takuboku.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.490
Erika, if you're going to tell her, at least tell her properly.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.700
Okay!

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.610
<i>Erika's the most popular girl in the class...</i>

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.500
<i>Compared to her, I'm just...</i>

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.910
<i>No, I can't be so negative! That'd be unfair to Erika!</i>

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.110
<i>Change! I'm going to change!</i>

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:22.580
Hey, why not come to my place today?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.800
I've got a great idea!

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.320
Let's go to Fairy Drop!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.930
Wow, these are really pretty!

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:36.570
We keep the accessories and all the small stuff on the first floor.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.470
Tsubomi!

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.640
Up here!

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.850
Now, what outfit do we go with...

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.890
Erika, what was the idea you had?

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.900
It's about recruiting for the Fashion Club.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.940
Wearing our school uniforms won't exactly be persuasive.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:53.660
Really, it'd be better if I designed something special, but I really don't have the time.{Changed 'specially' to 'special.' Could also do 'especially for it' but that's Too Damn Long.}

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.410
Do you think this'll do?

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.830
Huh? Do for what?

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.040
For you to wear, of course!

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.830
I think it'll suit you! Take a look!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.990
It's really too flashy for my tastes...

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:04.710
I guess.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.390
How about you pick one out?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.850
That one?

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:15.100
I've done some studying about color therapy. {They actually use the English term here, lol}

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.640
Apparently people tend to pick black and gray when they're feeling down.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.410
Are you feeling down, Tsubomi?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.140
You're... not completely off the mark.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.850
Then you should go for something green!

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:29.700
It'll ease your worries, and make you feel ready to try again!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.180
It's cute too, isn't it?

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:35.710
I don't think anyone will ever find out we're Precure,

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:39.810
but it'd be embarrassing to make our entrance without wearing cool clothes, right?!

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.370
I guess you're right...

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.670
If I don't, I guess I won't be worthy of teaming up with you, Erika...

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.610
Tsubomi!

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.090
Huh?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.410
Let's go for a run!

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:50.340
What?!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.750
Wh-Why are we running?!

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.010
Something bad's happened to you, hasn't it?

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:58.450
It's times like this when you just need to get on your feet and move!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.180
I'll run along with you!

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:03.040
Well, um... I dunno if I'd call it something bad...

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.150
What do you mean?!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.140
It's Mao and Ayumi.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.190
Are they students here?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.880
Yeah, they're really good.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.410
They made nationals in doubles.

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:17.700
Mao!

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:19.860
Erika...

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:20.700
What's the matter?

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.160
Ayumi says she wants to train on her own for a while.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:29.900
I'm always relying on Ayumi in our matches, so she probably got fed up with me.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.170
So if she stops playing with me, she can partner up with someone better...

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.670
<i>With someone better?!</i>

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.050
What, that's it?!

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.610
Why don't you just partner up with someone better too?

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.310
Partner up with someone else?!

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:46.080
<i>I'm going to go be a Precure with someone else, Tsubomi.</i>

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.900
If you start talking like that, Mao's gonna...

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.690
You have to look toward the future!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.930
Your partnership dissolving is a new start!

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:58.160
Partnership dissolving...

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.700
That's enough! Just leave me alone!

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.500
What's wrong with her?

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.500
Hey, Tsubomi!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.140
Huh?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:11.880
Tsubomi!

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.090
Wait! What's the matter with you?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.050
We might not have known each other very long...

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:18.180
Huh?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.190
But when you do find someone else...

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.620
please don't forget about me!

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.350
What're you saying?!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.350
Tsubomi!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.080
Are our Precures already splitting up? {Changed 'breaking apart' to 'splitting up.'}

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.020
That mustn't happen!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.710
Tsubomi's so weird!

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.250
Why'd she get so depressed all of a sudden? I don't get it.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.170
You stuffing yourself full of candy again?

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.660
Momo!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:58.640
You have a photo shoot here?

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:00.840
I've got a gravure shoot for a fashion magazine today.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.970
Though I'm on my break right now.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.890
Did you fight with Tsubomi again?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:07.640
We didn't fight!

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.300
This other girl was feeling down, so I just gave her some advice...

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:14.100
and then Tsubomi got all depressed on me!

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:18.110
You do tend to spit things out without
 thinking about the people you're talking to.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.660
You need to be more careful.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.960
I just tried to get her to be more positive!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.120
Maybe so, but sometimes that can do more harm than good.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.870
Momoka! If you'd join us, please!

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.330
Okay!

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.670
Not everyone's like you, Erika.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.960
I know that already!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.950
I know that...

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.640
Master Coupe!

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.220
Why did I become a Precure?

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:51.180
I'm spineless, shy, and completely unathletic...

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.330
I have absolutely no right to be a Precure...

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:56.740
I...

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.650
Is it all right for me to cry?!

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.500
You're so nice and fluffy...

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.610
Isn't he?

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.810
Grandma!

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.880
I did my best!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.090
Partnering up with another girl would just be cruel...

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:26.760
Who's there?!

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.720
I am a Commander of the Desert Apostles...

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.020
Kumojacky!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:37.930
The Flower of your Heart is about to wither, so I shall take it!

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.630
Flower of the Heart, show yourself!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.950
We won't be needing this.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.320
You're up, Desertrian!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.350
Roller!

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:08.680
This is bad!

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.310
We have to tell Tsubomi and Erika! {kisama yatsu-tachi}

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:14.990
Tsubomi,

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:18.880
if there were a "right" to be a Precure,

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.230
it would be due to having a strong and kind heart.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.570
To believe that everything is worth treasuring,

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.990
and to believe in your ability to keep trying, no matter how hard it gets.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:33.430
And you possess both of those traits, Tsubomi!

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:36.420
If it's you, Tsubomi, you can do it.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:37.780
Yes!

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:38.880
There's trouble!

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.190
A Desertrian's...

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.210
Tsubomi.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:49.410
Sheesh! I don't get Tsubomi <i>or</i> Momo!

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.070
Should I apologize?

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:52.100
But for what? {Removed 'if I should, then' - unnecessary.}

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.600
Here she is!

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.890
A Desertrian has appeared!

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:56.730
What?!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.440
Erika!

00:13:58.010 --> 00:13:58.940
Tsubomi...

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.400
Roller!

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:10.360
Mao's Flower of the Heart is the one that was stolen!

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:14.800
I worked so hard because I wanted to be doubles partners with Ayumi,

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:17.290
so why do I have to partner up with another girl?!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.690
At this rate, the Flower of Mao's Heart will wilt!

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:22.090
Let's hurry and restore it!

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:24.460
Got it!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:38.140
Seeds of the Precure, go forth!

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.500
Precure!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.420
Open My Heart!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.810
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:36.880
Cure Blossom!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.710
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.190
Cure Marine!

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.680
HeartCatch Precure!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:01.770
My partnership with Ayumi worked so well!

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.000
Blossom, let's go for a double punch!

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:04.980
Right!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.900
Double Precure...

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:10.780
I'm sorry!

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:14.620
You really <i>are</i> the weakest.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.980
You're... Kumojacky!

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:17.950
You two...

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.240
bore me!

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.330
Finish them!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:25.310
I'm sorry! All I do is hold you back, Marine...

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.840
That's not true!

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:33.340
Even though I practiced so hard so I wouldn't hold Ayumi back...

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.050
Marine!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.520
I'm causing you trouble again!

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:46.230
I really am no good!

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.780
You should partner up with someone better, Marine!

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:53.540
Wait, is that why you were so worried when I said she should partner with another girl?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.450
Yeah...

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:56.770
So that's what it was!

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:59.200
Why didn't you just say so?!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.950
If you don't tell me, there's no way I can understand!

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.460
So now you're <i>fighting</i>?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.330
Not only are you the weakest, but your partnership is also a disaster!

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:09.550
We aren't the weakest!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.670
We're the greatest partnership!

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.420
I like Blossom!

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.180
She's clever, really perceptive, and brilliant!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:19.890
Marine!

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:25.840
I'm sure that we need each other's strengths!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.580
And Chypre's too!

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:29.020
Coffret's too!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:37.950
Both of us are Precure!

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.020
We are Precure... {If we can find Arienai's font I want to sub this with it and extend to "We are Pretty Cure." It's clearly a reference to the old 'Futari wa Precure' naming format and I'd love to extend the reference.}

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.620
You... you really don't mind pairing up with me?

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.210
I don't mind at all!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.620
No, what I mean is...

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.290
It has to be you, Blossom!

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:49.250
Yes!

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:53.460
I have no time for your blabbering!{Changing BACK from I can't take your babbling anymore! BRITISH BRITISH CORRECT CORRECT. Changed from "I can't be doing with you babblers!"}

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:57.680
A man must weather alone the stormy seas of life!

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.640
This nonsense about "partnerships" and "not being alone" is nothing but foolishness!

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.390
It's not foolish at all!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.530
The desire people have to band together is precious!

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:13.400
You're just using Mao's feelings to make that monster rampage...

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:17.740
I've had it up to here with this!

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.190
I'll listen to your whining once you've defeated him!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.290
Roller!

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:28.510
Use your combined attack!

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:30.750
Now that both of your hearts are as one...

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:34.250
You'll bring forth an ultra super attack!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:35.550
Marine!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:36.590
Let's do it!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.590
This is our combined power!

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:51.230
Gather, Floral Power!

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.650
Blossom Tact!

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.790
Marine Tact!

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:07.750
Gather, Dual Floral Power!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:13.860
Precure Floral Power Fortissimo!

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.400
Heart Catch!

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.090
How very interesting.

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.830
It seems I will have to stop referring to you as the weakest after all.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:51.040
You should become even stronger!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.510
And only then shall I defeat you.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:57.250
We must return the Flower of the Heart to her!

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.050
Mao... Mao!

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.100
This is...

00:20:11.570 --> 00:20:13.080
You scared me!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.520
When I came back to the court you were just lying here.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:19.860
Ayumi, I promise I'll practice harder, 

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:22.280
so please don't break up our doubles team!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.240
Huh? What are you saying?

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.740
That's my line!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:32.710
I thought that if I didn't sharpen my skills, you'd be the one to leave.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:36.460
So I thought I'd practice on my own for a while...

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:41.550
So I just assumed that you'd gotten fed up with me?

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:45.680
I assumed that's what you were doing too.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.210
We really are silly...

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:57.650
We didn't trust each other, so we made ourselves worry needlessly, didn't we? {Reworded so it flowed better.}

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.900
Let's stay together from now on!

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:04.570
Of course! After all, we're the greatest partnership there is!

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:08.530
Ayumi!

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:13.170
In the language of flowers, a
 tweedia means "a trusting heart."

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:15.090
By trusting in each other,

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:19.540
their friendship has become even
 stronger than it was before, hasn't it?

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.220
I think a Heart Seed is going to be born!

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:42.280
I think our friendship has become stronger too, hasn't it?

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:44.240
It has!

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.200
Well then, I guess that makes us best friends.

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.910
Huh? Best friends?

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:50.700
Right?!

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:53.660
Yeah! Best friends it is!

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:09.880
{ED}

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:18.900
HeartCatch!

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:21.820
HeartCatch!

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:24.780
HeartCatch!

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:27.700
HeartCatch Precure!

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:36.250
The flower blooms with an "Open sesame!"

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:39.210
In the wardrobe of my heart

00:22:39.760 --> 00:22:42.380
are all the things that a girl loves

00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:44.840
Look, they're packed in so tight

00:22:45.390 --> 00:22:48.260
My makeover was a huge success

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:50.810
thanks to this scrunchie and this frilly tunic!

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:53.810
Our girly showtime

00:22:54.190 --> 00:22:56.650
is about to begin!

00:22:57.150 --> 00:22:59.860
Is my coordination lookin' good today?

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.780
Shuffle! Colorful! Beautiful!

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:05.700
Mismatches are just part of my character v(^^)v

00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:07.240
We're pretty

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:09.040
at full bloom!

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:12.160
If you polish your heart

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:15.210
until it shines

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:16.750
Then even the darkness

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:21.040
will become a guiding light

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:24.010
So don't sulk

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:26.930
because a smile's the best!

00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:30.390
Let's make them bloom, facing the sun

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.600
The flowers of our hearts

00:23:35.270 --> 00:23:36.480
HeartCatch!

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:39.940
HeartCatch Precure!

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:44.360
<i>A most treacherous man has appeared!</i>

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.400
<i>Looking toward the back of his father, who sacrifices everything, even his family, for his ramen serves </i>

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:49.610
<i>to touch the young boy's heart! {Added comma after 'father.'}</i>

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:50.860
<i>Wait, it doesn't?!</i>

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:53.570
<i>Akira is sad because his father 
makes no time to play with him!</i>

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:56.620
<i>Be on your guard! They're here to take his weakened heart!</i>

00:23:57.230 --> 00:23:59.290
<i>The enemy this time is a real hottie! What do we do?!</i>

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:01.140
<i>How about we go grab some ramen ourselves?</i>

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:01.920
<i>What?</i>

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:03.630
HeartCatch Precure<i>:</i>

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:06.880
Rejected Ramen<i>!</i>

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:06.880
Rejected Ramen<i>!</i>

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:09.040
<i>We'll catch everyone's hearts!</i>
